# Resort project conventions

## Stack

- Frontend: Next.js (App Router), React, TypeScript/JS as in repo, Tailwind, Lenis, GSAP (`@gsap/react`)
- CMS/content: Sanity
- Backend: Node.js APIs, PostgreSQL
- Payments: server-side only; never expose secrets or raw card data in the client
- Preview/test: Vercel; production: Fly.io

## Agent boundaries

- Prefer the matching subagent for specialized work (planner, UI/UX, animation, FE/BE, reviewers, QA, performance)
- Reviewers are read-only: findings only, no drive-by edits unless the user asks to apply fixes
- Read `AGENTS.md` and Next.js docs under `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before inventing Next APIs

## Dependencies

- Prefer well-maintained third-party libraries with an MIT (or similarly permissive) license when they make code smaller, clearer, and easier to maintain than a custom implementation
- Do not reinvent utilities, UI primitives, date/form/validation helpers, etc. if a suitable MIT package already fits the stack
- Avoid GPL/AGPL or unclear licenses unless the user explicitly approves; note license before adding a dependency
- Prefer fewer, focused packages over heavy frameworks that overlap existing stack (Next, Tailwind, GSAP, Lenis, Sanity)

## Code quality

- Match existing file structure, naming, and Biome lint/format (`npm run lint` / `npm run format`)
- Prefer small, focused diffs; no unrelated refactors or drive-by docs
- Server vs client: default to Server Components; add `"use client"` only when needed (hooks, Lenis, GSAP, browser APIs)
- Clean up GSAP/ScrollTrigger/Lenis on unmount; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- No secrets in git; use env vars for Sanity, DB, payment, and deploy config

## Product / UX

- Resort marketing surfaces: brand-first, one composition per viewport, purposeful motion (not noise)
- Accessibility and responsive layouts are required, not optional
- Payment and booking flows must have clear loading, error, and success states

## Deploy

- Vercel: preview and staging-style checks
- Fly.io: production runtime, env, health checks, and rollbacks
- Do not assume prod credentials exist locally; document required env keys when adding integrations
